---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '@/components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import RedesignProjectSelection from '@/components/RedesignProjectSelection.astro';
---
<Layout title="Websites, software & practical automation — M3MM" description="M3MM builds business websites, useful software and practical automations. Explore the work, understand the roadmap and start a conversation." path="/">
<Header slot="header" path="/" />

<section class="m3-hero container-page" aria-labelledby="home-title"><div><p class="m3-eyebrow">Independent engineering · Atlanta</p><h1 id="home-title">Good ideas.<br/><span>Working systems.</span></h1><p class="m3-lede">A clearer website. Less repetitive work. Software that solves a real problem. M3MM connects the idea to the build—and the build to what comes next.</p><div class="m3-actions"><a class="m3-button primary" href="/contact" data-cta="home-start" data-section="hero">Let’s build something →</a><a class="m3-button" href="/projects" data-cta="hq-released" data-section="hero">Explore the work</a></div></div><aside class="m3-manifesto" aria-label="The M3MM approach"><div><span>01</span><strong>Modernize.</strong><p>Make the experience clearer.</p></div><div><span>02</span><strong>Mobilize.</strong><p>Put useful tools to work.</p></div><div><span>03</span><strong>Multiply.</strong><p>Build on what proves its value.</p></div></aside></section>
<div class="m3-band"><div class="container-page"><span>Business websites</span><span>Web applications</span><span>AI &amp; workflow automation</span><span>One engineer. Clear ownership.</span></div></div>
<section class="m3-section container-page" aria-labelledby="home-services"><div class="m3-section-head"><div><p class="m3-eyebrow">What we do</p><h2 id="home-services">Built around the job.<br/>Not the latest buzzword.</h2></div><a class="m3-link" href="/services" data-cta="home-services" data-section="services">Explore services →</a></div><div class="m3-grid"><article class="m3-card"><p class="m3-eyebrow">01 / Websites</p><h3>A stronger first impression.</h3><p>Clear service pages, credible project work and a contact path that makes sense on a phone.</p></article><article class="m3-card"><p class="m3-eyebrow">02 / Applications</p><h3>A tool for the actual work.</h3><p>Focused web apps and internal tools, with requirements and ownership defined before the build.</p></article><article class="m3-card"><p class="m3-eyebrow">03 / Automation</p><h3>Less work on repeat.</h3><p>Connect steps, reduce manual handoffs and keep human approval where it belongs.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="released" class="m3-section container-page" aria-labelledby="home-work"><div class="m3-section-head"><div><p class="m3-eyebrow">Selected work</p><h2 id="home-work">Real projects.<br/>Honest status.</h2></div><p>Client builds and product previews have different stages. A reachable preview is not an official release.</p></div><RedesignProjectSelection/><a class="m3-link" href="/projects" data-cta="home-all-projects" data-section="projects">Browse the complete public project directory →</a></section>
<section id="roadmap" class="m3-section container-page" aria-labelledby="home-roadmaps"><div class="m3-section-head"><div><p class="m3-eyebrow">What comes next</p><h2 id="home-roadmaps">Two roadmaps.<br/>Two clear purposes.</h2></div><p>The products we’re building and the infrastructure that supports them, kept separate.</p></div><div class="m3-grid two"><article class="m3-card"><p class="m3-eyebrow">The work</p><h3>Project Roadmap</h3><p>Official releases, testing previews and proposed next steps.</p><a class="m3-link" href="/roadmap" data-cta="hq-roadmap-full" data-section="roadmap">Open Project Roadmap →</a></article><article class="m3-card"><p class="m3-eyebrow">The foundation</p><h3>Infrastructure Roadmap</h3><p>A public view of reliability, recovery and capacity milestones.</p><a class="m3-link" href="/roadmaps/infrastructure" data-cta="home-infrastructure" data-section="roadmap">Open Infrastructure Roadmap →</a></article></div></section>
<section class="container-page m3-close"><div><p class="m3-eyebrow">A direct working relationship</p><h2>Start with the problem.</h2><p>Tell Michael what you’re building, what isn’t working, and what a useful result looks like.</p></div><a class="m3-button primary" href="/contact" data-cta="home-contact" data-section="closing">Start a conversation →</a></section>

<Footer slot="footer" path="/" />
</Layout>
